{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Job You Want", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Obstacles Along the Way", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Third Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - used to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - used to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - used to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - used to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to express regret.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had met</span> before, we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have had</span> you on sooner.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If we had met before, we would have had you on sooner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you had listened to it, you would have known that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had taken more computer courses in college, I would have been better off than I am now. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You would have also been better off if you had listened to your kids when they explained Facebook.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Continuous Tense vs. The Future Perfect Tense ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the<span class=\"italic\"> Future Continuous</span> tense to talk about actions that will be in progress at a particular time in the future.<br/>You can use the <span class=\"italic\">Future Perfect</span> tense to talk about an action in the future that will already be completed by a specific time in the future. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the Future Continuous is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + <span class=\"italic\">be</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Rita, you <span class=\"strong\">will be releasing</span> your fourth book on this subject.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> is similar to the Present Perfect tense, but your viewpoint is in the future instead of the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You can bring me the report at 8 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have arrived</span> at the office by then.  <br/>The plane will leave the airport at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the airport at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the plane <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the Future Perfect tense is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">have </span>+ past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">will have changed</span> their jobs several times in their lifetime.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "By the end of the program, you will have heard about job hunting techniques for later on in life and you will have heard from my guest, job hunting expert Rita MacNeil. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You will be starting your own podcast next month called \u201cYour Personal Best\u201d. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "People will have changed their jobs several times in their lifetime.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We will be coming back after these messages.  ", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to dive into", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to start something suddenly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Today we are going to dive into job hunting.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when dealing with obstacles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "far-reaching", "type": "name"}, {"content": "affecting many people or things ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a very far-reaching topic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "discrimination", "type": "name"}, {"content": "practice of discriminating", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You also write about age discrimination in the workplace.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to disclose", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reveal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My studies have disclosed that older individuals tend to spend twice as much time looking for jobs than younger people do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "acclimatize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become accustomed to a new climate or environment ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Not only discrimination, but having to acclimatize to the new technology.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "substantial", "type": "name"}, {"content": "considerable amount", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hello and welcome to \u201cPractical Advice\u201d, the show that gives you substantial advice about everything.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make plans for the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I think about my career analytically using the Future Present Perfect and Future Continuous.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a timeline for my goals.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give suggestions and advice to my partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a career plan for your current job or the job you are studying for.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Where would you like to be in 6 months, 1 year, 3 years?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What obstacles are in your way?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a career plan that describes what you will be doing or what you will have done. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your career plan to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your partner can give suggestions.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What obstacles can slow a job search?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How can you overcome these obstacles?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "What obstacles are in your way?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selecte